      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berkeley_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Berkeley Township was incorporated as a township by an act of the New Jersey Legislature on March 31, 1875, from portions of Dover Township (now Toms River Township).",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berkeley_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The developers immediately began construction of the Pinewald pavilion and pier at the end of Butler Avenue.",
